---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Playground — Quire"
  description="Drop a .docx and the browser renders it with the same Rust engine, compiled to WebAssembly. Skeleton page: the interactive build is in progress."
  path="/playground"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="tick">●</span> WASM Playground — in progress</p>
      <h1>Drop a <code>.docx</code>. Render it in your browser.</h1>
      <p class="sub">
        The plan: the same Rust core as the CLI, compiled to <code>wasm32-unknown-unknown</code>,
        running entirely in your tab — no upload, no server, the bytes never leave the page.
        That render isn't wired up yet; the section below says what works and what doesn't.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="dropzone">
      <span class="chip">Engine loading</span>
      <p class="dz-title">Drop your file here</p>
      <p class="dz-sub">
        The interactive shell is being wired to the engine build. This page is the
        skeleton: the drop zone and its contract are real, the render is not yet.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.95rem;">
      The zone above is a placeholder, not a broken control: it accepts no files yet and
      never claims to have rendered one.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="spec-h">
    <h2 id="spec-h">What the playground will do</h2>
    <table class="spec">
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Input</th>
          <td>A local <code>.docx</code>, read in-tab with the File API. Nothing is uploaded.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Engine</th>
          <td>The <code>shells/web</code> wasm build — a thin adapter over the same core the CLI uses, streamed on first load with progress reported.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Output</th>
          <td>Line-break points and page splits from the real layout pass: shaped advances against real font metrics, Knuth-Plass breaks, pagination per <code>sectPr</code> geometry.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Editing</th>
          <td>An invisible caret at the engine's caret rectangle, so text entered through an IME lands where the engine thinks the cursor is and reflows incrementally.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Budget</th>
          <td>First wasm payload stays under its gzip budget in CI; the collaboration layer is a separate deferred chunk.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="status-h">
    <h2 id="status-h">Status</h2>
    <p>
      Not interactive yet. The engine work behind it — dual-target build, bundle split,
      size gate, caret contract — has landed; wiring the drop zone to a live render is a
      separate task. Until then, mail
      <a href="mailto:preview@quireoffice.dev">preview@quireoffice.dev</a> for a build to
      try.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
